      "description": "Watch Debreceni VSC vs FC Copenhagen highlights and goals from UEFA Europa Conference League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 6, 2026. The atmosphere in the UEFA Conference League was thick with anticipation as both sides prepared to battle for control of the pitch. Every challenge felt significant, with the tie hanging in the balance from the moment the whistle blew. Clinical execution in the first half On August 6, 2026 , FC Copenhagen arrived with a clear intent to dictate the tempo. Their persistence paid off in the 21st minute when Gabriel Pereira rose highest to meet a pinpoint cross from Marcos Lopez , nodding the ball home to break the deadlock. Debreceni VSC struggled to find a foothold, and their frustration manifested in aggressive play, leading to yellow cards for both Sohan Baldoni and Blaz Boskovic . The visitors remained composed and clinical; in the 35th minute, Robert doubled the lead with a sharp right-footed strike, leaving the hosts with a mountain to climb before the interval. Tactical management and late brilliance As the second half unfolded, the tactical battle intensified with a flurry of substitutions from both benches. Debreceni VSC looked to inject fresh energy through players like Balazs Sain and Botond Vajda , but FC Copenhagen remained structurally sound. The visitors managed the clock effectively despite a late yellow card for William Clem in the 80th minute. Any lingering hope for a comeback was extinguished in stoppage time when Andreas Cornelius headed in a cross provided by Mohamed Elyounoussi in the 91st minute, adding a final flourish to a dominant performance."
